{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1523343-question-about-piskey-mimic-ability","id":1523343,"title":"Question about Piskey mimic ability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-30T02:01:44-07:00","id":1523343,"title":"Question about Piskey mimic ability","content":"The ability of Piskey to mimic is quite confusing to me.<br /> <br /> Basically, a caucasian Piksey among hispanic people will look hispanic himself, but then this ability affects the Piskey's mortal body as well?<br /> <br /> Aslo, this mimic skill is something that the Piskey can control, or it's activation is automatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T22:43:16-07:00","id":1523389,"title":"","content":"It's described as an illusion, so I'd say it doesn't affect their body at all, it's just something people see. So a piskey travelling with bodybuilders would look big but could still squeeze into places the rest of the group couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T05:05:59-07:00","id":1523403,"title":"","content":"But even normal humans are affected by it?<br /> <br /> And if I'm going to play a Piskey in a chronicle, how my character will appear to the motley?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 10-01-2023, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T13:20:51-07:00","id":1523432,"title":"","content":"Well of course for any chronicle you\u2019re playing in the most important answer is that you\u2019ll need to talk with your ST about how they understand the rule and how they want to handle it.<br /> <br /> That said, here\u2019s my interpretation of the \u2018Blending In\u2019 birthright:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Piskie\u2019s mortal body does not actually change but the Piskie\u2019s chimerical self automatically produces an illusion which causes the Piskey to blend in with their (social) surroundings. This illusion is so powerful that only other changelings and supernaturals have the opportunity to see through it. So even if a Piskie\u2019s mortal body was born Asian, if they were walking through a Mexican market they would appear not only to Hispanic but of the same social position as most other market-goers.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Piskie\u2019s mortal body does not actually change but I would rule that physical interactions with mortals match what the mortals believe should be there; so a pipsqueak Piskie among bodybuilders would feel like they have a big body if hugged, even though their actual mass has not changed.<br /> <br /> \u2022I would rule that the Piskie cannot control their Illusion. Imo part of the RAW thematics of the Piskie is how mercurial their true self is.<br /> <br /> \u2022Amongst other Changelings the Piskie\u2019s appearance is still mutable and changing. However amongst the same group the \u2018most comfortable and convenient\u2019 appearance may become relatively consistent. Amongst most Changelings the Piskie will probably show their pointed ears but in mixed company they might not (and if surrounded by Pooka they might appear to have cat ears). If I had to guess most Piskey wear some chimerical item to help be recognized by other changelings, although even this could potentially be overlooked. However changelings do have the ability to make Perception + Kenning checks if they suspect someone is a Piskey to attempt to recognize them despite the illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T13:39:58-07:00","id":1523433,"title":"","content":"Basically if I have an ogre and a pooka in my party, my character could look like an ogre with cat ears and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T13:45:19-07:00","id":1523434,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s something for the ST and player to figure out tbh<br /> <br /> While that\u2019s a funny image, if I were running it I\u2019d probably have both players of the pooka and Ogre describe what their typical Changeling looks like and have the Piskey appear to be a mean of those two images","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T20:13:45-07:00","id":1523587,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is to make you seem &quot;typical&quot;, not average. You take on the characteristics the members of the group *share*. In the motley example, if the other members don't have any significant shared characteristics then there is no &quot;typical&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T01:19:39-07:00","id":1523612,"title":"","content":"I could see an argument that the Piskey already looks like a typical member of his own motley.<br /> <br /> Of course if they then travelled somewhere the rest of them looked out of place, he would change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}